From 7a10ee89c4379f362d55f5ecff7a2e8747fee5e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:32:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(metrics): include open intervals in thread accounting
 snapshots [daveey]

A scope crossing the first snapshot books pre-window CPU when it closes, yielding a negative interval residual. Keep an open interval registry and overlay its union at the same native-thread sampling boundary as completed accounting. Serialize entry/close/sampling; preserve completed loop counters and nested subtraction. Retain Linux tick-granular split beside the high-resolution total.

Proof: deterministic old-code pair produces -0.08 seconds residual; nested open control also fails. Nine accounting files pass including native Linux interval and close serialization controls; 26 surrounding consumer files pass 465 tests. Four exact-anchor mutants fail named tests (open term, inner subtraction, union root, sampling lock); full scripts/check passes21 gates. Phase2 WIP: further boundary failure-path coverage and report/wait reductions remain before publication. No Mac sample, PR or acceptance claim.
